  "sections": {
    "campaignRhythm": {
      "body": "Early play should alternate between consolidation and exposure. Build just enough to endure, then step back into the desert for resources that might let the colony last."
    },
    "openingDays": {
      "body": "The starting loadout gives the player meaningful capability without erasing pressure. There is enough equipment to act, enough water to plan, and enough sandwalking to make movement choices feel informed rather than random."
    },
    "premise": {
      "body": "This scenario is not a generic crashlanding transplanted onto a desert tileset. It is a survival start built around the systems the mod wants to foreground: water discipline, carried reserves, stillsuits, spice temptation, and maker threat."
    },
